<title>SPAIN: Spanish cash deficit conversion into nat/account.</title>
<headline>Spanish cash deficit conversion into nat/account.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Spanish government released the following table to explain the differences between the budget deficit on a cash basis and the budget deficit on a national account basis.</p>
<p>Data refer to the first four months in the year, accumulated until April (in billions of pesetas).</p>
<p>    1. Deficit on cash basis			     - 453.8</p>
<p>    2. Adjustments					   - 101.0</p>
<p>	  - variations in accrued revenues</p>
<p>	     and expenditures				  438.5</p>
<p>	  - Adj for state debt interest payments	  77.9</p>
<p>	  - Privatisations				   - 505.0</p>
<p>	  - Others					     - 112.4</p>
<p>    PSBR (1 + 2)					     - 554.7</p>
<p>    GDP estimation for 1997			     78,860.0</p>
<p>    As a percentage of GDP				     0.7%</p>
<p>NOTE - Spanish deficit on a national account basis up to March was standing at 836 billion pesetas, or 1.1 percent of the same GDP estimation.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
</text>
